 "title": "Sch9 and TORC1 Regulate pH Homeostasis and Cell Viability in Yeast",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the yeast organism and its regulation of pH homeostasis and cell viability. The Sch9 and TORC1 genes/proteins play crucial roles in this process, influencing various other genes/proteins such as PKA, V-ATPase, and Pma1. The yeast's regulation of pH homeostasis is also affected by external factors like nitrogen limitation and stress. Additionally, the cluster includes various cellular components like the ER, vacuole, and mitochondria, which interact with each other and with the yeast's regulatory mechanisms. The cluster also touches on the role of autophagy in regulating Sch9 and the involvement of rapamycin in inhibiting V-ATPase.",
